.\" File: man/mount_femtofs.8
.\" Created by Andrea "Nemesi" Cocito on 08/11/2026
.\" FemtoFS mount helper manual.
.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_FEMTOFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_femtofs
.Nd mount a resident FemtoFS bank
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar label directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility mounts an existing resident bank at
.Ar directory ,
which must already exist.
Load the module and populate the bank with the boot loader or
.Xr femtoctl 8
first.
The
.Ar label
is a bank name, not an image or device pathname.
Mounting requires root privileges.
.Pp
The filesystem is always mounted read-only.
Only one independent mount may claim each bank.
Unmount with
.Xr umount 8 ;
the bank remains available until explicitly discarded.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-o options"
.It Fl o Ar options
Comma-separated mount options; may be repeated.
The mutually exclusive
.Cm clean
(default) and
.Cm leaking
options control page-tail exposure as described in
.Xr femtofs 5 .
Generic read-only mount options such as
.Cm ro , noexec , nosuid
are also accepted.
The helper rejects
.Cm bank
and
.Cm from
options because the positional label supplies the bank selector.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kldload femtofs
femtoctl add data /path/to/data.0fs
mount_femtofs -o ro,clean data /mnt
umount /mnt
femtoctl discard data
.Ed
.Pp
An equivalent
.Pa /etc/fstab
entry, after bank registration, is:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
data /mnt femtofs ro,clean 0 0
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr femtofs 5 ,
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr femtoctl 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr umount 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Andrea \(dqNemesi\(dq Cocito - blackye at gmail dot com
